WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.880
[ YouTube Learning ]

00:00:03.020 --> 00:00:04.400
Now you are well aware of

00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:06.520
how you can communicate with your students

00:00:06.520 --> 00:00:07.740
through Google Classroom.

00:00:07.960 --> 00:00:11.060
But how can you share or create materials for them?

00:00:11.540 --> 00:00:12.600
Let’s explore!

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:17.140
[ Don't Memorise intro music ]

00:00:17.620 --> 00:00:19.400
Study materials could be information,

00:00:19.400 --> 00:00:21.040
or assignments or videos

00:00:21.400 --> 00:00:23.300
or even your pre-existing teaching aids

00:00:23.360 --> 00:00:25.180
you may have created earlier!

00:00:25.620 --> 00:00:28.120
For that we can access the Classwork tab

00:00:28.120 --> 00:00:28.940
you see here.

00:00:29.420 --> 00:00:30.780
You could first create a TOPIC

00:00:30.780 --> 00:00:32.840
that you want your students to understand,

00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:35.620
and add different kinds of materials to it.

00:00:36.500 --> 00:00:37.660
You can click here,

00:00:37.660 --> 00:00:39.420
and give a name to the topic.

00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:42.820
With that, you will see the name of your topic

00:00:42.820 --> 00:00:44.180
listed on the left here.

00:00:45.040 --> 00:00:47.520
Now let’s add some material to this topic.

00:00:48.980 --> 00:00:50.600
It’s crucial to give your material

00:00:50.600 --> 00:00:52.800
some appropriate title and description...

00:00:53.760 --> 00:00:54.760
Once you do that,

00:00:54.760 --> 00:00:56.880
you have an option to ADD some material

00:00:56.880 --> 00:00:58.460
that you have already prepared,

00:00:58.700 --> 00:01:00.480
or the option to create one.

00:01:01.620 --> 00:01:02.760
Let’s try creating

00:01:02.760 --> 00:01:04.940
or importing a Google Doc in this video,

00:01:05.080 --> 00:01:06.680
and in the upcoming videos,

00:01:06.720 --> 00:01:08.460
we can look at the other options!

00:01:09.160 --> 00:01:11.940
We can click on Create, and select Docs.

00:01:12.440 --> 00:01:14.640
And that will open a new Document.

00:01:15.300 --> 00:01:16.420
We can give it a name

00:01:16.420 --> 00:01:17.960
by editing this part here.

00:01:18.580 --> 00:01:21.120
Now most people assume that Google Docs

00:01:21.120 --> 00:01:23.120
is just about letters and words,

00:01:23.540 --> 00:01:24.260
but trust me,

00:01:24.300 --> 00:01:25.600
there’s lots more to it.

00:01:26.340 --> 00:01:28.180
Let me give you a few examples.

00:01:28.520 --> 00:01:29.840
You could click on Tools,

00:01:30.340 --> 00:01:31.700
select voice typing,

00:01:32.460 --> 00:01:34.820
select your language and see magic.

00:01:35.920 --> 00:01:37.620
We begin the recording now.

00:01:38.220 --> 00:01:41.920
“An equation says that two things are equal.

00:01:42.220 --> 00:01:43.200
Full stop.”

00:01:44.760 --> 00:01:46.600
And now we stop the recording.

00:01:47.060 --> 00:01:48.360
Interesting isn’t it?

00:01:48.700 --> 00:01:51.520
You can also insert an image from your computer.

00:01:51.900 --> 00:01:53.160
Or you could also search

00:01:53.160 --> 00:01:54.420
for an image on the web,

00:01:54.900 --> 00:01:57.160
select it, and add it to the document.

00:01:58.200 --> 00:02:01.600
You can also include equations and special characters.

00:02:02.860 --> 00:02:04.780
You could also redirect your students

00:02:04.780 --> 00:02:06.760
to an external website by inserting

00:02:06.760 --> 00:02:08.920
a link in the Doc… like this…

00:02:09.720 --> 00:02:11.800
But make sure you have vetted the website

00:02:11.800 --> 00:02:13.100
prior to sharing it.

00:02:14.480 --> 00:02:15.520
And guess what,

00:02:15.520 --> 00:02:17.580
you don’t need to keep saving it.

00:02:17.820 --> 00:02:19.780
It keeps getting auto-saved

00:02:19.780 --> 00:02:21.420
every time you add information.

00:02:21.900 --> 00:02:23.220
There are many more features,

00:02:23.220 --> 00:02:24.760
but we’ll keep that for later.

00:02:25.380 --> 00:02:28.240
We can now close the doc, by closing the tab.

00:02:28.860 --> 00:02:30.980
You will see your Google Doc here now.

00:02:31.500 --> 00:02:32.900
If you don’t see it updated,

00:02:32.900 --> 00:02:34.580
just refresh the page.

00:02:35.460 --> 00:02:37.200
You can then assign it to your topic

00:02:37.200 --> 00:02:39.280
by clicking here and selecting the topic.

00:02:40.080 --> 00:02:41.980
And you can choose if you want to share it

00:02:41.980 --> 00:02:43.180
with all your students,

00:02:43.280 --> 00:02:44.360
or just a select few.

00:02:46.120 --> 00:02:47.920
After you have added enough information,

00:02:48.020 --> 00:02:49.700
you can either post it immediately,

00:02:50.120 --> 00:02:52.040
or schedule it for a later date,

00:02:52.580 --> 00:02:54.100
or simply just save your information.

00:02:54.960 --> 00:02:56.240
Let’s post it for now.

00:02:57.180 --> 00:02:58.820
You can now see that the material

00:02:58.820 --> 00:03:00.500
will appear in your Stream Section.

00:03:00.940 --> 00:03:02.240
And your students as well

00:03:02.240 --> 00:03:04.240
will be able to see it in the Stream section!

00:03:05.240 --> 00:03:07.720
The good thing is that unless, you allow them,

00:03:07.720 --> 00:03:10.380
the students will not be able to EDIT your Docs

00:03:11.420 --> 00:03:12.800
They can just view them.

00:03:13.200 --> 00:03:14.680
That’s how easy it is to share

00:03:14.680 --> 00:03:16.440
a Google Doc file with your students.

00:03:17.540 --> 00:03:19.360
You can use Google Docs on any

00:03:19.360 --> 00:03:21.360
smartphone, laptop or tablet.

00:03:21.660 --> 00:03:23.580
You can even edit it while you are offline

00:03:23.580 --> 00:03:25.980
and it will sync changes once you go online.

00:03:27.340 --> 00:03:29.460
So Google Docs is one way in which

00:03:29.460 --> 00:03:31.460
you can share material with your students.

00:03:31.880 --> 00:03:33.500
Watch the next video to know

00:03:33.500 --> 00:03:35.660
how you could share beautiful presentations

00:03:35.660 --> 00:03:36.580
with your students!

00:03:36.840 --> 00:03:37.720
See you there!

00:03:38.220 --> 00:03:45.380
[ #TeachFromAnywhere ]

00:03:45.380 --> 00:03:48.000
[ YouTube Learning ]

